    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Generate a QR code file or terminal rendering for an authorization URL.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nPOSITIONALS:\r\n  url TEXT REQUIRED           Authorization URL to encode.\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -o,     --output TEXT       Output QR image path. .png and .svg write images; other\r\n                              extensions write text.\r\n          --ascii             Print a terminal QR code to stdout instead of writing an image\r\n                              file.\r\n          --size INT:INT in [64 - 4096] \r\n                              Target PNG edge length in pixels.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth qrcode 'https://example.com/verify' --output .tmp/login.png\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth qrcode 'https://example.com/verify' --ascii\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  This renders a generic URL QR code. For Jianying app scan login, use\r\n  `lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait` and render the returned qr_image_markdown.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Generate a QR code file or terminal rendering for an authorization URL.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nPOSITIONALS:\r\n  url TEXT REQUIRED           Authorization URL to encode.\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -o,     --output TEXT       Output QR image path. .png and .svg write images; other\r\n                              extensions write text.\r\n          --ascii             Print a terminal QR code to stdout instead of writing an image\r\n                              file.\r\n          --size INT:INT in [64 - 4096] \r\n                              Target PNG edge length in pixels.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth qrcode 'https://example.com/verify' --output .tmp/login.png\r\n  $ lyra-cli auth qrcode 'https://example.com/verify' --ascii\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  This renders a generic URL QR code. For Jianying app scan login, use\r\n  `lyra-cli auth login --qr-code --no-wait` and render the returned qr_image_markdown.\r\n",
